  "content": "Gold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\nOnlinekhabar\nMonday, October 6, 2025\n0\nComments\nPhoto: Unsplash/suradeach saetang\nKathmandu, October 6\nThe price of gold in the Nepali market has risen sharply by nearly Rs 10,000 per tola following the Dashain festival. During the holiday period, prices were not adjusted, but after the festival, a sudden revision led to a significant increase, according to the Federation of Nepal Gold and Silver Dealers’ Association.\nOn September 28 (Ashwin 12), gold was priced at Rs 223,200 per tola. After an increase of Rs 9,900, it reached Rs 233,100 per tola on Monday. Compared to Sunday, today’s price rose by Rs 2,500, as gold was traded at Rs 230,600 per tola the previous day. Today’s rate marks the highest gold price recorded so far.\nSimilarly, the price of silver has also gone up by Rs 150 per tola after Dashain. On Ashwin 12, silver was traded at Rs 2,810 per tola, which climbed to Rs 2,960 per tola on Monday. Compared to the previous day, the price of silver increased by Rs 30.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nNepal\nElection Commission\ncricket\nshare market\nroad\nGen Z\nMaitighar\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nGold price reaches record high at Rs 235,960 per tola\n2 days ago\nGold price reaches record high\n2 weeks ago\nGold price hikes by Rs 1,100 per tola\n3 weeks ago\nGold prices hit new record, rise by Rs 1,600 per tola\n1 month ago\nGold price hits record high at Rs 205,900 per tola\n1 month ago\nGold price hits record high, crosses Rs 200,000 per tola\n1 month ago\nMost Read\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\nFlood risks in Kathmandu, KMC launches helpline service\nCAA publishes domestic airfare rates, Kathmandu–Dhangadhi at Rs 17,579\nGold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n3 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n3 months ago\nAlso Read\nOpinion\nGen Z movement in Nepal at a crossroads: Between reform, revolt and reflection\n13 hours ago\nSociety\nDiversions built at 3 sections of BP Highway\n13 hours ago\nBlog\nHow Gen Z turned a hashtag into a revolution in Nepal\n13 hours ago\nPolitics\nElection Commission invites parties for talks on upcoming House election\n1 day ago\nSociety\nSeven charged in Pokhara Lichhibari land scam involving former ministers and officials\n1 day ago",
